# material written against it must still be STE-clean.
docs/reporting/feedback/2026-10-17-significant-external-review.md

# Extension (2026-10-19, hermes seat, room may flip): the D4 state-fed regen
# torque cap proposal is a dated plan record, amend-only as drafted — the sole
# copy of the κ-open proposal. New team material in it must still be STE-clean.
docs/plans/2026-10-07-state-fed-regen-cap-proposal.md

# Extension (2026-10-19, founder ruling, option A): the sweep stale-phrase
# extracts join the exempt class. A copy is a verbatim transcript of
# docs/agents/stale-phrases.md at one recorded revision: byte-identical, and
# that identity is its whole audit value. The class is transcript, not age
# and not generated data. The exemption is a pre-commit filter only: it
# removes the path from the linter argument list. ste-lint.py reads no
# exemption file, so a hand run still scores the transcript and fails. That
# direction is fail-safe, and no register line carries a prose score for
# these paths. The names are fixed permanently and carry no date, commit or
# sweep number; the sweep identity lives in the stamp file. The sweep writes
# both paths, so they are reserved names and absent before the first run.
scratch/sw_stale_phrases_base.md
scratch/sw_stale_phrases_tip.md

# Extension (2026-10-19, founder ruling, option A — third path): the sweep
# source register, docs/agents/stale-phrases.md, joins the amend-only class
# already carried here for DECISIONS.md and the trust log. It is the
# register the transcript class above copies. Measured against its own
# history (50e0300, b32bbb2): an entry is re-formed in place, and the change
# carries a dated "Note (YYYY-MM-DD):" line under the carrying entry, so no
# entry changes without a dated note. The file scores 3.21/100w whole-file
# against a 2.0 block, so an amendment cannot clear the gate on its own
# prose; the two commits that amended it held --no-verify for this class.
# New entries must still be STE-clean. The exemption is a pre-commit filter
# only: ste-lint.py reads no exemption file, so a hand run still scores the
# whole file and fails.
docs/agents/stale-phrases.md

# Extension (2026-10-20, builder seat, room may flip): the founder return
# registers are verbatim external records, the class carried here since
# 2026-10-14 for relayed feedback. Every table row quotes Rod's own comment
# word for word, contractions and long cells included. Rewriting a quote
# corrupts the record, and the register exists so the room can check it
# against the returned copy. The builder's own prose in the file measures
# 1.92/100w, under the 2.0 block. New team prose in the file must stay clean.
docs/reporting/feedback/2026-10-20-founder-return-3-comments.md
